BT /F1 16 Tf 54 748 Td (A Two-Period Directed-Search Model with Wealth Heterogeneity) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 720 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 708 Td (Equilibrium Definition and Numerical Solution) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 696 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 684 Td (Simplified version of Repele \(2026\): no heterogeneity in job type x.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 672 Td (All jobs have common productivity y_bar, separation probability delta,) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 660 Td (retention Delta = 1-delta, and vacancy cost phi.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 648 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 636 Td (Workers differ in initial liquid wealth a1 ~ G\(a1\). Preferences:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 624 Td (    u\(c1\) + beta E[u\(c2\)],   u' > 0, u'' < 0.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 612 Td (Savings satisfy a2 >= a_bar and earn gross return R.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 600 Td (All workers start period 1 unemployed; unemployment income in period 2 is b.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 588 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 576 Td (A submarket is indexed by posted wage w. Let n\(w\) be applicants and v\(w\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 564 Td (vacancies. In an active submarket:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 552 Td (    theta\(w\) = v\(w\) / n\(w\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 540 Td (Worker job-finding probability: p\(theta\), increasing in theta.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 528 Td (Vacancy-filling probability: q\(theta\)=p\(theta\)/theta, decreasing in theta.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 516 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 504 Td (Period-2 values:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 492 Td (    E2\(a2,w\) = u\(R a2 + w\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 480 Td (    U2\(a2\)   = u\(R a2 + b\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 468 Td (    J\(w\)     = y_bar - w.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
