<< /Length 2152 >>
stream
BT /F1 16 Tf 54 748 Td (Why there is no fixed point over theta\(w\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 720 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 708 Td (Conditional on w, free entry determines theta\(w\) point by point:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 696 Td (    q\(theta\(w\)\) = phi / [ beta Delta \(y_bar-w\) ].) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 684 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 672 Td (Under CRS matching, firm profitability depends on n and v only through) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 660 Td (theta=v/n. It does not depend on the absolute mass or composition of applicants.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 648 Td (Thus the solution sequence is) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 636 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 624 Td (    w  ->  theta\(w\)  ->  worker choices  ->  n\(w\)  ->  v\(w\)=theta\(w\)n\(w\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 612 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 600 Td (A genuine fixed point would arise if firm profitability depended on the) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 588 Td (endogenous composition of applicants \(for example worker productivity types\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 576 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 564 Td (MATCHING-FUNCTION PARAMETERIZATION \(Repele 2026, Appendix B1\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 552 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 540 Td (    M\(n,v\) = n v \(n^gamma + v^gamma\)^\(-1/gamma\), gamma>0.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 528 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 516 Td (With theta=v/n:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 504 Td (    p\(theta\) = theta \(1+theta^gamma\)^\(-1/gamma\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 492 Td (    q\(theta\) =       \(1+theta^gamma\)^\(-1/gamma\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 480 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 468 Td (Define) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 456 Td (    q_FE\(w\) = phi / [ beta Delta \(y_bar-w\) ].) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 444 Td (For 0<q_FE\(w\)<1, free entry can be inverted analytically:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 432 Td (    theta\(w\) = \( q_FE\(w\)^\(-gamma\) - 1 \)^\(1/gamma\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 420 Td (Then p\(w\)=p\(theta\(w\)\). If q_FE\(w\)>=1, the submarket is inactive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 408 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 396 Td (Repele's quantitative model uses gamma=0.38. Her quantitative model also) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 384 Td (uses CRRA sigma=2; both are natural benchmark values for a numerical example.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
13 0 obj
<< /Length 2079 >>
stream
BT /F1 16 Tf 54 748 Td (Numerical parameterization and grids) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 720 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 708 Td (Normalize y_bar=1. Choose beta and R consistently with the period length.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 696 Td (Choose common delta and set Delta=1-delta. A simple benefit rule is) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 684 Td (    b = rho_b y_bar.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 672 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660 Td (CALIBRATING VACANCY COST.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 648 Td (Pick reference wage w_ref and target job-finding probability p_ref.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 636 Td (For the matching function above:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 624 Td (    theta_ref = [p_ref^gamma/\(1-p_ref^gamma\)]^\(1/gamma\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 612 Td (    q_ref     = \(1-p_ref^gamma\)^\(1/gamma\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 600 Td (    phi       = beta Delta q_ref \(y_bar-w_ref\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 588 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 576 Td (WAGE GRID.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 564 Td (Active submarkets require q_FE\(w\)<=1, hence) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 552 Td (    w <= y_bar - phi/\(beta Delta\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 540 Td (With no nonpecuniary value of employment, w<=b is dominated. Use) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 528 Td (    w_min = b + eps_w) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 516 Td (    w_max = y_bar - phi/\(beta Delta\) - eps_w.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 504 Td (A uniform grid with about 200-500 points is adequate.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 492 Td (Because theta\(w\) can vary rapidly near w_max, an alternative is a grid) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 480 Td (uniform in theta or p, recovering wages from) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 468 Td (    w\(theta\) = y_bar - phi/[beta Delta q\(theta\)].) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 456 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 444 Td (WEALTH GRID.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 432 Td (With a_bar=0, use a1 in [0,a_max], concentrated near zero:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 420 Td (    a1_i = a_max [\(i-1\)/\(N_a-1\)]^kappa,  kappa>1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 408 Td (For illustration, kappa=2 and N_a around 200 are adequate.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 396 Td (Attach masses mu_i from a parametric or empirical liquid-wealth distribution.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
