BT /F1 16 Tf 54 748 Td (Solution algorithm) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 720 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 708 Td (Step 1. Choose wage grid {w_j}, wealth grid {a1_i}, and masses {mu_i}.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 696 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 684 Td (Step 2. For each wage w_j compute) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 672 Td (    q_FE_j = phi/[beta Delta \(y_bar-w_j\)].) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 660 Td (If 0<q_FE_j<1, compute theta_j from the analytical inversion and) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 648 Td (p_j=p\(theta_j\). Otherwise mark the submarket inactive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 636 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 624 Td (Step 3. For each pair \(a1_i,w_j\), solve the one-dimensional savings problem) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 612 Td (over a2:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 600 Td (    max u\(R a1_i-a2\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 588 Td (        + beta p_j Delta u\(R a2+w_j\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 576 Td (        + beta \(1-p_j Delta\) u\(R a2+b\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 564 Td (A convenient feasible interval is [a_bar, R a1_i-eps_c].) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 552 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 540 Td (Step 4. For each wealth type, choose the wage index j*\(i\) giving the) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 528 Td (largest optimized value. Store w_i*, theta_i*, p_i*, and a2_i*.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 516 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 504 Td (Step 5. Count applicants:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 492 Td (    n_j = sum_i mu_i 1{j*\(i\)=j}.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 480 Td (This is the mass of period-1 searchers in the submarket, not an unemployment rate.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 468 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 456 Td (Step 6. Set vacancies in each active submarket:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 444 Td (    v_j = theta_j n_j.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 432 Td (If n_j=0, set v_j=0.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 420 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 408 Td (Step 7. Verify free entry, theta_j=v_j/n_j, and worker optimality.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 396 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 384 Td (Output: a1 -> \(a2*\(a1\),w*\(a1\),theta*\(a1\),p*\(a1\)\), plus n\(w\),v\(w\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 372 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 360 Td (REFERENCE) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 348 Td (Repele, Amalia \(2026\), Wealth Sorting and Cyclical Employment Risk,) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 336 Td (Job Market Paper, International Institute for Economic Studies,) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 324 Td (Stockholm University, July 2026.) Tj ET
endstream
